WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.784 --> 00:00:11.318
Each week page is a complete module: what to read, what the ideas mean, and ways to check yourself. Weeks open folded so you can see the whole shape first.

2
00:00:11.318 --> 00:00:22.329
Start with the hero card. It names the week's question, how the week runs, and a Start button that drops you at the right first section. Live weeks also carry a class recording and updates section.

3
00:00:22.329 --> 00:00:33.156
Open sections one at a time. Up to two sections stay open at once, and Collapse all folds the page back up. The In this week rail jumps straight to any section.

4
00:00:33.156 --> 00:00:44.161
Rate the ideas in Before you begin. Mark each idea New to me, Getting it, or I can. You rate the same ideas again at the end of the week to see how far your understanding moved. There is no grade, just your own read.

5
00:00:44.161 --> 00:00:55.165
Read the week through your selected route. The Learning emphasis section rewrites the week's concepts, terms, and reading order through your route. The required source set never changes: on every route you work the Western reading and the named Indigenous scholar together, each kept whole and attributed.

6
00:00:55.165 --> 00:01:06.166
Do the activity and enter the weekly experience. The activity turns the week's ideas into decisions you make yourself, and the experience opens the week's interactive world. Both support the readings; neither replaces them.

7
00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:17.173
Rehearse with the Study Guide, then take the Knowledge Check. The guide flips terms from earlier weeks, asks you to explain ideas back, and climbs a question ladder. The check has three sets: A and B are multiple choice with an honest confidence rating, and Set C brings scenarios, matching, and short written answers you rate yourself. The report names your confident misses; review those first.

8
00:01:17.173 --> 00:01:28.225
Close with the reflection and Generate Your Weekly Notes. Type your reflection, then generate the Word file. It gathers your check answers, activity summary, and reflection into one record on Seneca letterhead.

9
00:01:28.225 --> 00:01:38.491
Every check on this page is practice. None of it is scored, recorded, or visible to your professor. Blackboard is the official channel for graded work.

10
00:01:38.491 --> 00:01:44.172
Where next: When the week feels solid, return Home and open the next station.
